# The Recoil engine release the rjm-bar-host image is built from.
#
# This is BAR's *official* Linux build, downloaded and checksum-verified, not a
# source build: a lobby host must run the same engine as the players who join
# it, and a simulation result is only meaningful against what people play.
# It must match the engine the BAR launcher currently installs
# (data/engine/recoil_<version>/ on a player's machine).
#
# Custom Skirmish AIs are built elsewhere (the AI's own repository, e.g.
# S3KCentrifugal/CircuitAI's release workflow) and installed at container start.
# An AI's libSkirmishAI.so should be built against this engine's headers; see
# design section 3 for what a mismatch looks like.
#
# Changing these is an engine upgrade: a reviewed diff, never incidental drift.
# ENGINE_SHA256 is the sha256 of recoil_<version>_amd64-linux.7z from
# https://github.com/beyond-all-reason/RecoilEngine/releases/tag/<version>.
ENGINE_VERSION=2026.07.04
ENGINE_SHA256=9824c2c38124e4b90a9b5f7c4e7200c3ea6503c0bd4bff0e0ff46212ec29dcab
